WEBVTT


00:00:47.548 --> 00:00:50.467
Queen to the king,
possible straight going there.


00:00:50.551 --> 00:00:53.804
Eight on the eight.
And the jack gets a boss.


00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:56.932
Eights open.


00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:02.479
Aren't you guys afraid of an officer
coming down here or something?


00:01:02.563 --> 00:01:05.524
Trust me.
Nobody ever comes down here but us.


00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:10.988
- That thing always do that?
- Do what?


00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.240
Whatever that thing is under the tarp.


00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:15.576
I thought I just saw it move,
or do something...


00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.954
Probably the only thing
it ever did was cost money.


00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:21.498
I'm telling you, the thing is moving!


00:01:21.582 --> 00:01:24.334
If you don't have the straight, just fold.


00:01:58.035 --> 00:01:59.828
What are you doing?


00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.700
Hold your fire!


00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:30.669
This is Area C.


00:03:30.752 --> 00:03:33.255
We're under heavy fire down here.
We need...


00:03:50.314 --> 00:03:51.648
To the gate room!


00:03:51.732 --> 00:03:53.483
Go, go, go! Move it!


00:04:15.506 --> 00:04:17.049
Hold your fire!


00:05:12.229 --> 00:05:14.982
I thought I saw someone on
the roof when we came up the drive, sir.


00:05:15.065 --> 00:05:17.192
There's a ladder over there.


00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:32.541
- Colonel Jack O'Neill?
- Retired.


00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.626
I'm Major Samuels.


00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.546
Want a little piece of advice, Major?


00:05:38.255 --> 00:05:42.050
Get re-assed to NASA.
That's where all the action's gonna be.


00:05:43.302 --> 00:05:44.636
Out there.


00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:50.559
I'm... I'm under orders to bring you
to see General Hammond, sir.


00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:53.937
- Never heard of him.
- He replaced General West.


00:05:54.021 --> 00:05:56.982
- I'm a busy man, Major.
- I can see that, sir.


00:05:57.399 --> 00:05:59.318
He says it's important.


00:05:59.526 --> 00:06:01.653
Has to do with the stargate.


00:06:52.788 --> 00:06:54.957
We have to take a second elevator
the rest of the way, sir.


00:06:54.998 --> 00:06:56.834
It's a long way down.


00:06:57.167 --> 00:07:00.420
Yeah, I know. I've been here before.


00:07:01.338 --> 00:07:02.798
Of course.


00:07:18.605 --> 00:07:20.107
This way, sir.


00:07:35.122 --> 00:07:36.248
Come.


00:07:36.623 --> 00:07:39.293
General Hammond, Colonel Jack O'Neill.


00:07:39.751 --> 00:07:41.003
Retired.


00:07:42.045 --> 00:07:44.590
I can see that. I envy you, Colonel.


00:07:45.632 --> 00:07:48.510
Major Samuels mentioned something
about the stargate.


00:07:48.552 --> 00:07:52.055
Down to business. I can do that.
This way...


00:08:01.607 --> 00:08:03.609
Anyone you know, Colonel?


00:08:03.901 --> 00:08:05.569
They're not human.


00:08:05.903 --> 00:08:07.237
You think?


00:08:08.572 --> 00:08:11.158
Best we can tell,
these slits are actually a pouch,


00:08:11.241 --> 00:08:13.452
similar to that found in a marsupial.


00:08:13.535 --> 00:08:15.120
- Like a kangaroo.
- Mmm.


00:08:15.996 --> 00:08:17.247
Except...


00:08:23.253 --> 00:08:24.796
In both sexes.


00:08:25.589 --> 00:08:29.051
These people, or aliens,
whatever you wanna call them,


00:08:29.134 --> 00:08:32.387
came through, killed four of my people


00:08:32.471 --> 00:08:35.516
and kidnapped another,
using advanced weapons.


00:08:36.099 --> 00:08:37.267
Airman?


00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:38.852
Weapons?


00:08:50.697 --> 00:08:52.783
Seen one before, I take it?


00:08:53.492 --> 00:08:54.743
Yes, sir.


00:08:55.744 --> 00:08:57.663
But there are no creatures like this
on Abydos.


00:08:57.746 --> 00:09:00.749
Those people were human.
They were from Earth.


00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:02.835
Ra brought 'em there
thousands of years ago.


00:09:02.918 --> 00:09:04.795
I know all about that.


00:09:05.379 --> 00:09:08.715
But your report said this Ra was in fact


00:09:08.799 --> 00:09:11.510
some kind of alien that lived
inside a human body.


00:09:11.593 --> 00:09:14.304
His eyes glowed. That was our first clue.


00:09:18.308 --> 00:09:20.686
Are you sure he's dead, Colonel?


00:09:22.062 --> 00:09:24.314
Unless he could survive a tactical
nuclear warhead


00:09:24.398 --> 00:09:27.901
blowing up in his face, I'm positive. Why?


00:09:28.527 --> 00:09:32.656
Well, Colonel, these people,
or whatever they are,


00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:36.785
were guarding another man
who retreated back through the stargate.


00:09:37.077 --> 00:09:40.581
I got a good look at his eyes, Colonel.
They glowed.


00:09:47.504 --> 00:09:50.924
How do you feel about the Stargate
mission after all this time, Colonel?


00:09:51.008 --> 00:09:52.426
How do you mean?


00:09:52.509 --> 00:09:55.137
Well, it's been over a year.
Has your perspective changed?


00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:56.805
Well, sir, I...


00:10:04.271 --> 00:10:06.940
Kawalsky and Ferretti? Yes.


00:10:07.191 --> 00:10:09.985
Served under your command
on the first Stargate mission.


00:10:10.027 --> 00:10:11.862
Have a seat, Colonel.


00:10:18.535 --> 00:10:21.288
Tell me about Daniel Jackson, Colonel.


00:10:21.455 --> 00:10:23.707
Why are they questioning my men?


00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:26.752
They're not your men anymore, Colonel.
You retired.


00:10:26.835 --> 00:10:28.420
Daniel Jackson?


00:10:30.881 --> 00:10:32.633
- You read the report?
- Yes.


00:10:32.716 --> 00:10:34.593
- It's all there.
- Is it?


00:10:37.596 --> 00:10:39.598
What's this all about, General?


00:10:39.681 --> 00:10:42.142
You didn't like Daniel Jackson, did you?


00:10:42.226 --> 00:10:44.186
Basically, he was a geek, sir.


00:10:44.228 --> 00:10:45.854
So you didn't have a lot of time for him?


00:10:45.938 --> 00:10:47.606
I didn't say that.


00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.692
He also saved my life and found
the way home for my men and me.


00:10:50.734 --> 00:10:53.237
A little thing like that can kind of
make a person grow on you.


00:10:53.278 --> 00:10:54.530
According to the mission brief,


00:10:54.571 --> 00:10:57.032
your orders were to
go through the stargate,


00:10:57.074 --> 00:11:01.912
to detect any possible threat to Earth,
and if found, to detonate a nuclear device


00:11:01.995 --> 00:11:03.914
and destroy the gate on the other side.


00:11:03.997 --> 00:11:05.040
Yes.


00:11:05.082 --> 00:11:07.376
But that's
not what you did, is it?


00:11:07.459 --> 00:11:09.044
Not right away.


00:11:09.294 --> 00:11:13.882
Ra's forces overpowered my team
and took the weapon before I could arm it.


00:11:14.508 --> 00:11:16.969
But, with Dr. Jackson's help,
you eventually regained control,


00:11:17.052 --> 00:11:19.847
- and did, in fact, detonate the weapon?
- Yes.


00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:23.350
So, to the best of your knowledge,
Daniel Jackson and everyone else


00:11:23.433 --> 00:11:26.019
you knew on Abydos is dead, correct?


00:11:26.937 --> 00:11:28.397
That's correct.


00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:29.565
Good.


00:11:29.773 --> 00:11:33.443
Then you won't mind if I authorize
a go-ahead on our plan.


00:11:40.284 --> 00:11:44.246
This quartz material
the stargates are made of,


00:11:44.329 --> 00:11:47.291
it must be tough stuff
if it can withstand a Mark 3.


00:11:47.374 --> 00:11:50.335
Well, we sent a robot probe through
after we got back, sir.


00:11:50.419 --> 00:11:52.462
It was flattened on the other end.


00:11:52.546 --> 00:11:56.341
Obviously, the Abydos stargate
had been buried in the rubble.


00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:58.969
But somehow, it got unburied.


00:12:05.225 --> 00:12:06.643
Oh, my God!


00:12:09.313 --> 00:12:10.606
You're sending another bomb?


00:12:10.689 --> 00:12:12.441
A Mark 5 this time.


00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:17.404
Unless you have something to add.


00:12:26.788 --> 00:12:28.624
General Hammond, sir.


00:12:32.336 --> 00:12:36.256
I regret to inform you that my report
was not entirely accurate.


00:12:36.548 --> 00:12:37.883
You didn't detonate the bomb.


00:12:37.966 --> 00:12:41.261
I did detonate the bomb, sir,
and it was aboard Ra's spacecraft,


00:12:41.345 --> 00:12:43.722
so it did kill him
and eliminate the risk to Earth.


00:12:43.805 --> 00:12:45.682
- However...
- However...


00:12:49.853 --> 00:12:53.190
Ra's ship was in orbit
above the planet at the time.


00:12:54.274 --> 00:12:58.195
Neither the gate nor anything else
on the planet was destroyed.


00:12:59.821 --> 00:13:02.574
Daniel Jackson is alive
and living with the people on Abydos.


00:13:02.658 --> 00:13:04.493
You violated direct orders. Why?


00:13:04.535 --> 00:13:06.328
Because the people of Abydos
are no threat to us.


00:13:06.411 --> 00:13:07.538
They deserve to be left alone.


00:13:07.621 --> 00:13:09.122
That's not up to you...


00:13:09.206 --> 00:13:12.334
If I'd come back here and reported the gate
on the other side was still intact,


00:13:12.417 --> 00:13:15.087
we would've sent another bomb,
just like you were about to.


00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.297
It wasn't necessary to let those people die.


00:13:17.381 --> 00:13:18.966
The threat from Ra was gone.


00:13:19.049 --> 00:13:22.177
What about the probe we sent through?
It was crushed instantly.


00:13:22.219 --> 00:13:24.888
After we came home,
Daniel buried the gate in rocks,


00:13:24.972 --> 00:13:28.016
making my return
or anybody else's impossible.


00:13:28.475 --> 00:13:31.937
Those four bodies lying in the infirmary
say otherwise.


00:13:35.232 --> 00:13:37.025
Take Colonel O'Neill to the holding room.


00:13:37.067 --> 00:13:41.071
Give him a little time to think about
things while I decide what to do with him.


00:13:42.239 --> 00:13:43.615
Sergeant.


00:14:02.092 --> 00:14:03.886
Colonel O'Neill, sir.


00:14:04.094 --> 00:14:06.847
I'm retired, Kawalsky. Lose the salute.


00:14:11.351 --> 00:14:14.188
Me and Ferretti didn't tell them anything.


00:14:14.771 --> 00:14:16.398
I appreciate that.


00:14:16.481 --> 00:14:19.401
Hey, those kids on Abydos
saved my life, too.


00:14:20.777 --> 00:14:22.613
Yeah. Those kids...


00:14:24.531 --> 00:14:27.701
I mean, they're the whole reason
we kept it secret.


00:14:27.951 --> 00:14:29.119
Right?


00:14:31.205 --> 00:14:33.916
That one kid idolized you. Remember him?


00:14:35.125 --> 00:14:36.668
Weird name... What was it?


00:14:36.752 --> 00:14:37.961
Skaara.


00:14:38.795 --> 00:14:39.922
Right.


00:14:40.464 --> 00:14:43.217
Remember how he was
always saluting you?


00:14:43.425 --> 00:14:44.510
Yeah.


00:14:45.427 --> 00:14:48.263
My kid used to do that when he was little.


00:14:49.598 --> 00:14:51.934
Skaara kind of reminded me of him.


00:15:01.068 --> 00:15:03.779
How many people did you say
are on Abydos?


00:15:03.862 --> 00:15:06.323
That we saw? Maybe 5,000.


00:15:13.497 --> 00:15:16.375
Does this mean you're reconsidering
sending the bomb, sir?


00:15:16.458 --> 00:15:18.836
It means I'm open to suggestions.


00:15:20.379 --> 00:15:23.882
General, let me take a team
through that gate.


00:15:24.675 --> 00:15:26.134
We'll find out who those aliens are.


00:15:26.218 --> 00:15:28.512
Kawalsky and I have been there before.
We know the lay of the land.


00:15:28.595 --> 00:15:29.596
We know the people.


00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.974
You think you know them.
Jackson could be dead.


00:15:32.015 --> 00:15:33.350
You don't know
what you'd be walking into.


00:15:33.433 --> 00:15:35.811
There is one way to find out, sir.


00:15:35.853 --> 00:15:38.480
We'll have the prototype probe
shipped from MIT.


00:15:38.564 --> 00:15:41.400
No, sir. We don't need that probe.


00:15:42.234 --> 00:15:44.403
- We don't?
- Nope. This'll do.


00:15:54.037 --> 00:15:55.831
Chevron one encoded.


00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:06.842
Chevron two encoded.


00:16:08.385 --> 00:16:10.262
Care to explain this concept?


00:16:10.345 --> 00:16:11.847
Chevron three encoded.


00:16:11.889 --> 00:16:13.765
Jackson has allergies.


00:16:14.683 --> 00:16:15.934
I get it.


00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.228
Chevron four encoded.


00:16:18.312 --> 00:16:21.690
He'll know this came from me
and not from someone like...


00:16:23.066 --> 00:16:24.359
Yourself.


00:16:26.195 --> 00:16:27.863
Chevron five encoded.


00:16:27.905 --> 00:16:29.698
Why not just send a note?


00:16:29.781 --> 00:16:31.700
- Anyone could send a note.
- Anyone could send a note.


00:16:40.751 --> 00:16:42.544
Chevron six encoded.


00:16:51.053 --> 00:16:52.846
Chevron seven locked.


00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.051
Now what?


00:17:31.343 --> 00:17:33.887
If Jackson's still around,
he'll know what the message means.


00:17:33.971 --> 00:17:36.014
What if the aliens got it?


00:17:36.098 --> 00:17:38.892
Well, they could be blowing
their noses right now.


00:17:38.976 --> 00:17:41.353
They could be planning an attack.


00:17:41.687 --> 00:17:45.190
Come on, Samuels.
Let me be the cynic around here, huh?


00:17:46.358 --> 00:17:48.861
General, this could take some time.


00:18:18.515 --> 00:18:19.892
Incoming wormhole.


00:19:05.479 --> 00:19:07.981
Permission to take a team through
the stargate, sir?


00:19:08.065 --> 00:19:10.567
Assuming I get
the President's authorization,


00:19:10.609 --> 00:19:12.861
the mission briefing will be at 0800 hours.


00:19:12.903 --> 00:19:16.198
Consider yourself recalled
to active duty, Colonel.


00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:45.185
Gentlemen, take your seats.


00:19:48.689 --> 00:19:49.857
Where's Captain Carter?


00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:51.441
Just arriving, sir.


00:19:51.525 --> 00:19:52.734
Carter?


00:19:52.943 --> 00:19:55.737
I'm assigning Sam Carter to this mission.


00:19:55.946 --> 00:19:58.323
I'd prefer to put together
my own team, sir.


00:19:58.407 --> 00:20:02.578
I'm sorry. Not on this mission.
Carter's our expert on the stargate.


00:20:03.829 --> 00:20:05.038
Where is he transferring from?


00:20:05.122 --> 00:20:07.749
She is transferring
from the Pentagon.


00:20:11.295 --> 00:20:13.130
I take it you're Colonel O'Neill.


00:20:13.213 --> 00:20:15.924
Captain Samantha Carter reporting, sir.


00:20:18.635 --> 00:20:20.804
But, of course, you go by Sam.


00:20:20.888 --> 00:20:22.181
Let's get started.


00:20:22.264 --> 00:20:24.016
- Colonel?
- All right.


00:20:24.683 --> 00:20:28.187
For those of you on your first trip
through the gate,


00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:30.105
you should be prepared
for what to expect.


00:20:30.189 --> 00:20:33.442
Well, I've practically memorized
your report from the first mission, sir.


00:20:33.483 --> 00:20:36.320
I'd like to think I've been
preparing for this all my life.


00:20:36.403 --> 00:20:38.030
I think what the Colonel is saying is,


00:20:38.113 --> 00:20:41.909
have you ever pulled out of a simulated
bombing run in an F-16 at eight-plus Gs?


00:20:41.992 --> 00:20:43.035
Yes.


00:20:46.079 --> 00:20:47.831
Well, it's way worse than that.


00:20:47.915 --> 00:20:50.918
By the time you get to the other side,
you're frozen stiff,


00:20:51.001 --> 00:20:52.878
like you've just been through a blizzard.


00:20:52.961 --> 00:20:55.255
That's a result of the compression
your molecules undergo


00:20:55.339 --> 00:20:57.549
during the millisecond required
for reconstitution.


00:20:57.633 --> 00:20:59.760
Here we go. Another scientist.


00:20:59.843 --> 00:21:01.303
General, please.


00:21:01.345 --> 00:21:03.096
Theoretical astrophysicist.


00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:04.473
Which means?


00:21:04.515 --> 00:21:07.309
Means she's smarter than you are, Colonel.


00:21:07.351 --> 00:21:10.354
Especially in matters
related to the stargate.


00:21:18.237 --> 00:21:22.658
Well, you can believe me, this has nothing
to do with you being a woman.


00:21:22.991 --> 00:21:24.451
I like women.


00:21:25.202 --> 00:21:27.871
I've just got a little problem
with scientists.


00:21:27.955 --> 00:21:32.376
Well, Colonel, I logged over 100 hours
in enemy airspace during the Gulf War.


00:21:32.459 --> 00:21:34.211
Is that tough enough for you?


00:21:34.294 --> 00:21:36.839
Or are we gonna have to arm wrestle?


00:21:40.884 --> 00:21:43.679
I don't mean to throw a damper
on your enthusiasm,


00:21:43.762 --> 00:21:45.764
but I still say the safest
and most logical way


00:21:45.848 --> 00:21:49.142
is to bury the stargate,
just like the ancient Egyptians did,


00:21:49.226 --> 00:21:51.645
make it impossible for the aliens to return.


00:21:51.728 --> 00:21:54.106
It's the only way to eliminate the threat.


00:21:54.189 --> 00:21:56.441
- Except it won't work.
- It worked before.


00:21:56.525 --> 00:21:59.862
How do you all think the stargate
got to Earth in the first place?


00:21:59.945 --> 00:22:01.029
Good question.


00:22:01.071 --> 00:22:02.865
They've got ships, General.


00:22:02.948 --> 00:22:05.701
Ra had one as big as the great pyramids.


00:22:05.742 --> 00:22:10.539
They don't need the stargate to get here.
They can do it the old-fashioned way.


00:22:10.747 --> 00:22:15.502
Now, with all due respect
to Mr. Glass-Is-Half-Empty over here,


00:22:15.586 --> 00:22:17.546
don't you think maybe
we should use the stargate


00:22:17.588 --> 00:22:21.592
to do a little reconnaissance
before they decide to show up again?


00:22:33.103 --> 00:22:37.858
I'll give you exactly 24 hours to either
return or send a message through.


00:22:37.941 --> 00:22:39.902
No Kleenex boxes, please.


00:22:39.985 --> 00:22:43.906
Otherwise, I will assume the worst,
and send a bomb through.


00:22:44.114 --> 00:22:45.491
Understood.


00:23:03.550 --> 00:23:06.637
- Try to follow orders this time, Colonel.
- Sir?


00:23:06.720 --> 00:23:10.182
This time, you bring Daniel Jackson back.
Is that clear?


00:23:12.392 --> 00:23:13.602
Move out!


00:23:28.826 --> 00:23:31.703
My God! Look at this!


00:23:32.371 --> 00:23:36.208
You can actually see the fluctuations
in the event horizon.


00:24:51.200 --> 00:24:52.784
Lower your guns.


00:25:03.420 --> 00:25:06.715
Hello, Jack. Welcome back.


00:25:21.396 --> 00:25:23.190
- Skaara.
- O'Neer.


00:25:26.944 --> 00:25:29.696
I did not think to be seeing you again.


00:25:35.035 --> 00:25:36.245
How are you, Daniel?


00:25:36.286 --> 00:25:37.663
Good. You?


00:25:38.580 --> 00:25:41.500
Much better, now that I know
everybody's okay.


00:25:41.583 --> 00:25:44.002
Greetings from Earth, Dr. Jackson.


00:25:44.294 --> 00:25:45.879
Hello, Ferretti.


00:25:45.963 --> 00:25:48.340
Brought you a little something, Daniel.


00:25:48.423 --> 00:25:49.758
Kawalsky.


00:25:52.302 --> 00:25:54.096
Sha're, don't be shy.


00:25:57.474 --> 00:25:59.393
It's good to see you again.


00:26:03.605 --> 00:26:05.357
So, I figured it was only a matter of time


00:26:05.440 --> 00:26:07.901
before you had to tell the truth
about us still being here.


00:26:07.985 --> 00:26:09.111
Yeah.


00:26:09.319 --> 00:26:11.488
Why the militia?
Something else come through?


00:26:11.572 --> 00:26:15.075
- No, we're just taking precautions. Why?
- Amazing.


00:26:15.159 --> 00:26:18.120
This is what was missing
from the dig at Giza.


00:26:19.371 --> 00:26:21.081
This is how they controlled it.


00:26:21.165 --> 00:26:23.667
It took us 15 years
and three supercomputers


00:26:23.750 --> 00:26:26.336
to jury-rig a control system
for the gate on Earth!


00:26:26.420 --> 00:26:28.672
- Captain.
- Look how small it is!


00:26:28.755 --> 00:26:30.007
Captain!


00:26:30.090 --> 00:26:31.091
Oh.


00:26:32.676 --> 00:26:33.969
Right.


00:26:37.222 --> 00:26:39.183
Dr. Jackson, I presume.


00:26:40.184 --> 00:26:41.768
I'm Dr. Samantha Carter.


00:26:41.852 --> 00:26:42.811
Hi.


00:26:45.480 --> 00:26:47.316
What's going on, Jack?


00:26:49.526 --> 00:26:52.321
Six hostile aliens came through
the stargate on Earth.


00:26:52.404 --> 00:26:54.948
Four people are dead, one's missing.


00:26:55.199 --> 00:26:56.617
One of them looked like Ra, Daniel.


00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:59.077
Well,
they didn't come from here.


00:26:59.745 --> 00:27:02.164
I mean, the boys take shifts guarding it,
36 hours a day, every day.


00:27:02.206 --> 00:27:04.833
We'd know if they came through here.


00:27:04.917 --> 00:27:09.213
Well, they came from somewhere, Daniel.
I'm gonna have to look around.


00:27:11.173 --> 00:27:12.758
I think I can help you find out who it was,


00:27:12.841 --> 00:27:16.220
but it's going to have to wait
till the sandstorm is over.


00:27:17.471 --> 00:27:21.350
We were about to have our evening meal.
Why don't you join us?


00:27:40.077 --> 00:27:43.705
I'm sure the folks at MIT would be happy
to know their million-dollar probe


00:27:43.747 --> 00:27:45.666
also makes fine cookware.


00:27:45.749 --> 00:27:50.003
Well, it got pretty banged up when it came
through the gate into our barricade,


00:27:50.087 --> 00:27:54.508
so we made use, and...
Well, it is non-stick titanium, so it...


00:27:58.679 --> 00:28:00.347
Very good. Perfect.


00:28:00.430 --> 00:28:02.641
Beanaa wa. Everybody try this.


00:28:03.892 --> 00:28:05.185
This too.


00:28:08.730 --> 00:28:10.107
What's this?


00:28:12.109 --> 00:28:13.277
Drink.


00:28:16.613 --> 00:28:20.242
Moonshine? Did you make this?


00:28:20.701 --> 00:28:21.743
Moonshine?


00:28:21.785 --> 00:28:24.037
Yeah, moonshine. As in booze.


00:28:25.205 --> 00:28:27.749
Daniel, what are you teaching these kids?


00:28:27.833 --> 00:28:30.878
Our little soldiers
are all grown up, Colonel.


00:28:31.837 --> 00:28:33.046
Try it.


00:28:35.132 --> 00:28:39.761
All right. Skaara's moonshine.
Let's give it a shot.


00:28:41.972 --> 00:28:43.223
Oh, God!


00:28:48.812 --> 00:28:50.856
Smooth. Very smooth.


00:28:51.440 --> 00:28:52.691
Moonshine.


00:28:53.901 --> 00:28:55.360
I'm so proud.


00:28:56.153 --> 00:28:57.154
Wow!


00:28:57.571 --> 00:28:58.906
O'Neer...


00:29:02.951 --> 00:29:05.579
No. It's yours.


00:29:06.830 --> 00:29:09.416
I gave that to you to keep. Remember?


00:29:11.418 --> 00:29:12.753
Thank you.


00:29:18.509 --> 00:29:22.930
You know, he's never had that out of his
sight the whole time you were gone.


00:29:23.013 --> 00:29:24.097
Yeah?


00:29:26.475 --> 00:29:31.188
So this man who looked like Ra,
he must've come through another gate.


00:29:31.271 --> 00:29:32.481
- What other gate?
- Another stargate?


00:29:32.564 --> 00:29:35.901
- The stargate only goes here.
- No. No. I think you're wrong about that.


00:29:35.984 --> 00:29:38.153
I was there.
We ran hundreds of permutations.


00:29:38.195 --> 00:29:40.280
But you didn't have what you need.


00:29:40.364 --> 00:29:42.324
Daniel, what are you talking about?


00:29:42.366 --> 00:29:44.910
Daniel, the storm has passed.


00:29:45.619 --> 00:29:47.120
I'll show you.


00:29:47.204 --> 00:29:50.666
Sha're, ben qua ri Jack and his
friends to see the vili tao an.


00:29:51.750 --> 00:29:53.752
No, no, I won't be long.


00:30:11.061 --> 00:30:12.771
Goodbye, my Daniel.


00:30:18.902 --> 00:30:20.153
Goodbye.


00:30:21.405 --> 00:30:22.489
Bye.


00:30:44.511 --> 00:30:47.639
- I can't say I missed this place.
- Come on.


00:30:49.892 --> 00:30:53.520
- This is just incredible.
- You ain't seen nothing yet.


00:31:07.784 --> 00:31:09.244
Let go of me!


00:31:10.120 --> 00:31:12.539
Where the hell are you taking me?


00:31:16.710 --> 00:31:17.711
Come.


00:31:18.795 --> 00:31:19.922
Let go of me.


00:31:21.798 --> 00:31:24.176
Lovely. Full of life.


00:31:30.641 --> 00:31:33.602
You could be the vessel
for my future queen.


00:31:38.315 --> 00:31:40.442
Yes. Very nice, indeed.


00:31:42.569 --> 00:31:45.531
But I am not the one
you must finally please.


00:32:57.186 --> 00:32:58.437
A shame.


00:33:24.046 --> 00:33:25.506
So, I figured that
there had to be


00:33:25.589 --> 00:33:28.634
more to this place, so I started exploring.


00:33:28.717 --> 00:33:30.719
Just the area around the town
and the pyramid, at first.


00:33:30.802 --> 00:33:32.554
Then after about a month,
I found this place.


00:33:32.596 --> 00:33:34.932
Doctor, you're gonna love this.


00:33:37.017 --> 00:33:38.393
Oh, my God!


00:33:39.686 --> 00:33:42.940
This is the archeological find
of the century. There must be...


00:33:43.023 --> 00:33:45.359
Thousands of lines of hieroglyphs.


00:33:45.442 --> 00:33:49.571
So, Daniel, have you had a chance
to translate this yet?


00:33:49.655 --> 00:33:51.990
- I think so.
- What's it say?


00:33:53.534 --> 00:33:55.994
Well, it doesn't say anything.


00:33:56.370 --> 00:34:00.749
Actually, it's sort of a chart,
more of a map.


00:34:00.791 --> 00:34:01.959
A map?


00:34:03.961 --> 00:34:05.087
Of?


00:34:06.380 --> 00:34:07.631
Well, I haven't been able
to analyze all of it.


00:34:07.714 --> 00:34:11.301
I mean, look at it.
It would take my whole life.


00:34:11.385 --> 00:34:14.263
Well, Daniel, we don't have
that much time.


00:34:15.305 --> 00:34:16.890
What's it a map of?


00:34:16.974 --> 00:34:19.768
Well, the cartouches seem to be
separated clearly into groupings.


00:34:19.810 --> 00:34:22.437
Each grouping is attached to the others
with a series of lines.


00:34:22.521 --> 00:34:24.648
And each grouping of glyphs
contain seven symbols.


00:34:24.731 --> 00:34:26.608
So you can see where
this is going, of course.


00:34:26.692 --> 00:34:28.944
Why don't you tell us anyway?


00:34:30.237 --> 00:34:32.823
All the symbols are on
the stargate in the Abydos chamber.


00:34:32.906 --> 00:34:36.243
I've also managed to chart
some of them in the Abydos night sky,


00:34:36.326 --> 00:34:38.328
or at least pretty close.


00:34:38.704 --> 00:34:43.625
I think that this is a map of
a vast network of stargates.


00:34:43.667 --> 00:34:46.170
Stargates that are all over the galaxy!


00:34:46.253 --> 00:34:48.672
I don't think that can be, Doctor.


00:34:49.840 --> 00:34:51.133
Why not?


00:34:51.675 --> 00:34:54.052
Well, because after Colonel O'Neill
and his team came back,


00:34:54.136 --> 00:34:56.138
my team ran hundreds
of symbol permutations,


00:34:56.221 --> 00:34:59.099
using Earth as the point of origin,
and it never worked.


00:34:59.183 --> 00:35:01.977
Then where did your Ra lookalike
come from?


00:35:05.105 --> 00:35:07.191
Look, I don't pretend to know
anything about astrophysics,


00:35:07.274 --> 00:35:09.067
but couldn't the planets change?


00:35:09.151 --> 00:35:14.531
I mean, drift apart or something
like that to throw this map off?


00:35:15.699 --> 00:35:17.910
- I knew I'd like you.
- Really?


00:35:18.994 --> 00:35:21.872
I mean... You mean, I'm right?


00:35:22.289 --> 00:35:23.582
The galaxy is a vortex.


00:35:23.665 --> 00:35:26.418
All the stars are constantly moving
in relation to one another.


00:35:26.502 --> 00:35:28.420
So in the thousands of years
since the stargate was built...


00:35:28.504 --> 00:35:29.671
All the coordinates could've changed.


00:35:29.713 --> 00:35:32.007
But why does it still work
between Abydos and Earth?


00:35:32.090 --> 00:35:34.718
Well, Abydos is probably the closest
planet in the network to Earth.


00:35:34.801 --> 00:35:37.596
I mean, the closer they are, the less
the difference in relative position.


00:35:37.679 --> 00:35:39.765
The further away,
the greater the difference.


00:35:39.848 --> 00:35:42.518
In a few thousand more years, it won't
work between Earth and Abydos either.


00:35:42.601 --> 00:35:44.186
Unless you can adjust
for the displacement.


00:35:44.269 --> 00:35:46.855
Right. Now, with this map as a base,
that should be easy.


00:35:46.939 --> 00:35:49.358
All we have to do is correct
for stellar drift.


00:35:49.441 --> 00:35:51.610
Then, I should be able to arrive
at a computer model


00:35:51.693 --> 00:35:55.113
that will predict the adjustments
necessary to get the gate working again.


00:35:55.197 --> 00:35:59.368
So the stargate can go other places?


00:35:59.409 --> 00:36:01.495
- Well, yes. Yes, it could.
- Probably.


00:36:01.578 --> 00:36:05.415
Sir, with your permission, I'd like to put
this entire cartouche on digital video.


00:36:05.499 --> 00:36:08.043
Then, when we get back to Earth,
I can download it into the computer


00:36:08.126 --> 00:36:09.545
and get faster results.


00:36:09.628 --> 00:36:11.129
Yeah, go ahead.


00:36:34.069 --> 00:36:37.906
Man, you gotta give Daniel credit.
She is one beautiful woman.


00:36:46.373 --> 00:36:47.499
Go, go, go.


00:38:01.114 --> 00:38:04.618
This is not your weapon.
Where did you get it?


00:38:16.964 --> 00:38:18.841
A good choice, Teal'c.


00:38:19.299 --> 00:38:21.009
A perfect specimen.


00:38:38.485 --> 00:38:40.237
You may be the one.


00:39:33.624 --> 00:39:34.791
Sha're!


00:39:42.174 --> 00:39:43.675
Hey, what's up, guys?


00:39:43.759 --> 00:39:46.053
I wonder if he saw the symbols.


00:39:47.554 --> 00:39:48.722
Bolaa!


00:39:51.517 --> 00:39:54.311
It's all right. Just tell me what happened.


00:39:54.645 --> 00:39:56.021
It was Ra.


00:39:56.230 --> 00:39:57.314
Okay. Okay.


00:39:59.816 --> 00:40:01.026
Hang in there, Ferretti.


00:40:01.109 --> 00:40:02.736
- What's going on?
- Ra is dead.


00:40:03.570 --> 00:40:07.950
No... Ra, I saw... He took Sha're.


00:40:08.367 --> 00:40:10.828
He took Skaara into the chaapa 'ai.


00:40:13.205 --> 00:40:15.958
Where? Did you see?
Show me the pictures.


00:40:16.542 --> 00:40:17.960
Did you see?


00:40:27.594 --> 00:40:28.804
Come on.


00:40:32.516 --> 00:40:34.935
What's going on, Daniel?
Could there be another Ra?


00:40:35.018 --> 00:40:36.812
How in the hell should I know?


00:40:36.854 --> 00:40:39.565
I should have left the barricade up.
This is my fault.


00:40:39.648 --> 00:40:41.984
Colonel, Ferretti needs
medical attention now!


00:40:42.025 --> 00:40:43.902
Go! Help him. I can send you back.


00:40:43.986 --> 00:40:46.655
You're coming with us this time, Daniel.
I've got orders.


00:40:46.738 --> 00:40:49.199
I don't care about your orders, Colonel.


00:40:49.283 --> 00:40:50.784
My wife is out there. So is Skaara.


00:40:50.868 --> 00:40:53.912
And the only way we're gonna get 'em
back is for you to come home with us.


00:40:53.996 --> 00:40:56.498
Ferretti might have
seen those coordinates.


00:40:56.582 --> 00:40:58.667
I've got everything I need.


00:41:22.774 --> 00:41:25.360
After we go through the chaapa 'ai,


00:41:25.444 --> 00:41:29.490
you have to bury it like we did before,
and then leave this place.


00:41:30.991 --> 00:41:32.743
- You come back?
- No.


00:41:33.994 --> 00:41:35.329
No, I can't. Nobody can.


00:41:35.412 --> 00:41:39.208
That's what I'm telling you.
Not for a long time.


00:41:40.083 --> 00:41:42.669
Now, as soon as we're gone,
I want you to close it. Bury it.


00:41:42.753 --> 00:41:44.963
Put a big, heavy cover stone over it.


00:41:45.047 --> 00:41:46.632
Nothing good can ever
come through this gate.


00:41:46.715 --> 00:41:48.383
Do you understand?


00:41:50.260 --> 00:41:52.471
You came through it, Daniel.


00:41:56.391 --> 00:41:58.977
Do you remember the story I told you?


00:42:00.103 --> 00:42:02.648
How the ancient Egyptians back on Earth
cut themselves off from Ra?


00:42:02.731 --> 00:42:05.567
Well, that is exactly what you have to do.


00:42:07.444 --> 00:42:10.697
Then, in one year, one year from this day,
you take the cover stone away.


00:42:10.781 --> 00:42:13.700
I will try to bring Sha're home
with me on that day.


00:42:13.784 --> 00:42:16.578
But if I don't make it back, if I don't...


00:42:16.620 --> 00:42:19.998
If I don't return, then you must
bury the gate again forever, joa qua?


00:42:23.794 --> 00:42:25.128
Promise me.


00:42:25.295 --> 00:42:26.463
- Yes.
- Yes.


00:42:27.464 --> 00:42:29.174
We promise, Daniel.


00:42:32.636 --> 00:42:35.430
You tell Sha're's father, in one year...


00:43:02.791 --> 00:43:06.253
Incoming wormhole.
Stand by for arrival.


00:43:29.359 --> 00:43:31.653
Close the iris! Close the iris!


00:43:44.082 --> 00:43:45.918
What the hell's that, sir?


00:43:46.001 --> 00:43:49.129
That's our insurance against
any more surprises.


00:43:53.550 --> 00:43:55.052
What happened, Colonel?


00:43:55.135 --> 00:43:57.763
Base camp was hit while
we were on recon, sir.


00:43:57.846 --> 00:44:00.682
Ferretti's hurt,
Currin and Swope are down.


00:44:00.849 --> 00:44:02.768
Same hostiles who attacked us?


00:44:02.851 --> 00:44:04.561
That's a fair guess.


00:44:04.645 --> 00:44:07.814
Jackson's wife and one of our kids
was kidnapped.


00:44:08.524 --> 00:44:10.609
General, hi. I'm Daniel Jackson.
We've never met.


00:44:10.692 --> 00:44:13.862
I'd like to be on the team
that goes after them.


00:44:13.904 --> 00:44:17.199
You're not in any position
to make demands, Jackson.


00:44:24.498 --> 00:44:26.124
Ferretti might have seen
the sequence of symbols


00:44:26.208 --> 00:44:27.876
they used to go through the stargate.


00:44:27.918 --> 00:44:30.170
That should tell us where they went.


00:44:30.254 --> 00:44:34.132
General, Dr. Jackson found
an entire cartouche on Abydos


00:44:34.216 --> 00:44:37.094
with 1,000 possible coordinates,
maybe more.


00:44:37.594 --> 00:44:39.513
That's 1,000 new worlds, General.


00:44:39.596 --> 00:44:42.266
And our stargate can take us
to these worlds?


00:44:42.349 --> 00:44:45.060
With this new data, as long as we make
the appropriate allowances


00:44:45.102 --> 00:44:46.520
for alignment in the targeting computer...


00:44:46.603 --> 00:44:47.896
Yes or no?


00:44:48.772 --> 00:44:50.566
I think so, sir. Yes.


00:44:50.732 --> 00:44:54.194
Request permission to upload the symbols
into the base supercomputer for analysis.


00:44:54.278 --> 00:44:57.990
And, sir, I'd like to lead the rescue mission
once we find out where these hostiles are.


00:44:58.073 --> 00:45:01.326
We'll discuss that request in a briefing
at 0800 hours.


00:45:01.410 --> 00:45:04.121
Captain Carter, the base computer
is at your disposal.


00:45:04.204 --> 00:45:08.000
In the meantime, get this man
some clean clothing. He stinks.


00:46:00.552 --> 00:46:02.638
Your death cannot help her.


00:46:04.556 --> 00:46:06.475
I am not afraid of you!


00:46:27.120 --> 00:46:28.121
No!


00:46:47.307 --> 00:46:49.434
Doc says he's gonna make it.


00:46:51.603 --> 00:46:52.855
Yes, sir.


00:46:55.524 --> 00:46:58.193
- You gonna stay here all night?
- Yes, sir.


00:47:19.840 --> 00:47:20.924
Hey.


00:47:24.136 --> 00:47:26.638
They don't know what to do with me.


00:47:27.139 --> 00:47:29.892
And I don't know what to do with myself.


00:47:34.313 --> 00:47:36.482
Come on. Let's get out of here.


00:47:57.127 --> 00:47:58.754
- Nice catch.
- Thank you.


00:47:58.795 --> 00:48:02.257
Sorry. Gate travel always seems
to make my allergies...


00:48:08.222 --> 00:48:10.891
- Sorry.
- So, you were saying...


00:48:11.058 --> 00:48:12.559
Anyway...


00:48:13.602 --> 00:48:15.229
As soon as you were gone
and they realized they were free,


00:48:15.312 --> 00:48:18.649
I mean, Abydos was
their world for the taking.


00:48:19.566 --> 00:48:23.445
- Had a little party, did you?
- Yeah. Yeah, big, big party.


00:48:23.821 --> 00:48:28.492
They treated me like their savior.
It was embarrassing.


00:48:29.284 --> 00:48:31.870
Savior of Abydos? Doesn't sound so bad.


00:48:31.954 --> 00:48:35.791
Yeah, I spent the first year having to stop
everyone I saw from bowing all the time.


00:48:35.874 --> 00:48:37.918
It's amazing you turned out so normal.


00:48:38.001 --> 00:48:40.963
Well, if it wasn't for Sha're, I probably...


00:48:47.177 --> 00:48:48.846
She was the complete opposite
of everyone else.


00:48:48.929 --> 00:48:51.014
She practically fell on the floor
laughing every time


00:48:51.098 --> 00:48:54.059
I tried to do some chore
they all took for granted.


00:48:54.142 --> 00:48:57.104
Like, grinding yaphetta flour.


00:48:58.522 --> 00:49:01.859
I mean, have you ever tried
to grind your own flour?


00:49:02.234 --> 00:49:04.778
I'm trying to kick the flour thing.


00:49:06.029 --> 00:49:08.490
This is going straight to my head.


00:49:09.908 --> 00:49:12.327
What time is it anyway?
I must have gate-lag or something.


00:49:12.411 --> 00:49:15.497
Daniel, for crying out loud,
you've had one beer.


00:49:15.581 --> 00:49:17.166
You're a cheaper date than my wife was.


00:49:17.249 --> 00:49:20.002
Yes, when am I going to meet your wife?


00:49:21.712 --> 00:49:24.923
Probably never.


00:49:29.052 --> 00:49:33.265
After I came back from Abydos
the first time, she'd already left.


00:49:35.475 --> 00:49:38.270
- I'm sorry.
- Yeah. So was I.


00:49:41.106 --> 00:49:44.109
I think in her heart she forgave me
for what happened to our kid.


00:49:44.193 --> 00:49:46.862
She just couldn't forget.


00:49:48.322 --> 00:49:50.073
And what about you?


00:49:50.991 --> 00:49:54.995
I'm the opposite. I'll never forgive myself.


00:49:57.581 --> 00:49:59.708
But sometimes, I can forget.


00:50:12.763 --> 00:50:16.725
People, what is spoken of in this room
is classified as SCI, top secret.


00:50:17.059 --> 00:50:20.354
Colonel, what do we know about
these hostiles we didn't yesterday?


00:50:20.437 --> 00:50:21.980
Not a hell of a lot, General.


00:50:22.064 --> 00:50:26.610
The Abydon boys who survived the attack
on base camp thought it was Ra.


00:50:26.693 --> 00:50:28.070
I thought he was dead.
Gentlemen, which is it?


00:50:28.153 --> 00:50:29.446
He's dead. He's definitely dead.


00:50:29.530 --> 00:50:33.200
I mean, the bomb...
I mean, he's gotta be dead, right?


00:50:33.283 --> 00:50:35.410
- Then who's coming through the stargate?
- Gods.


00:50:35.494 --> 00:50:38.872
- What?
- Not as in "God" god.


00:50:38.956 --> 00:50:40.207
Ra played a god, the sun god.


00:50:40.290 --> 00:50:42.376
He borrowed the religion and culture
of the ancient Egyptians


00:50:42.459 --> 00:50:44.920
he brought through the gate,
and then he used it to enslave them.


00:50:45.003 --> 00:50:48.674
You see, he wanted the people of Abydos
to believe that he was the only one.


00:50:48.757 --> 00:50:51.385
You're saying
Ra's not the last of his race, after all?


00:50:51.468 --> 00:50:53.929
- Maybe he's got a brother, Ray.
- That's what we need.


00:50:54.012 --> 00:50:56.723
Wait a minute.
The legend goes, Ra's race was dying.


00:50:56.807 --> 00:50:59.309
He survived by taking over the body
of his human host, an Egyptian boy.


00:50:59.393 --> 00:51:01.979
But who's to say more of his kind
couldn't do the same thing?


00:51:02.062 --> 00:51:05.065
I mean, this could have happened
at any time, anywhere there's a gate.


00:51:05.149 --> 00:51:07.484
I mean, this could be happening right now.


00:51:07.568 --> 00:51:10.112
Colonel, you've had the most experience
in fighting this hostile.


00:51:10.195 --> 00:51:13.490
Assuming you have to defend yourself
in the field, are you up to it?


00:51:13.574 --> 00:51:15.450
- We beat 'em once.
- I'll take that as a maybe.


00:51:15.492 --> 00:51:18.245
Captain Carter, you're confident
that the stargate will take us


00:51:18.328 --> 00:51:20.372
where we want to go
with this new information?


00:51:20.455 --> 00:51:22.291
Well, the computer's feeding
the revised coordinates


00:51:22.332 --> 00:51:24.126
into the targeting computer right now.


00:51:24.209 --> 00:51:25.586
It'll take time to calculate,


00:51:25.669 --> 00:51:28.172
but it should spit out
two or three destinations a month.


00:51:28.255 --> 00:51:29.715
Let's not fool ourselves here, people.


00:51:29.798 --> 00:51:33.135
This thing is both vast and dangerous,
and we are in so far over our heads


00:51:33.177 --> 00:51:34.595
we can barely see daylight.


00:51:34.678 --> 00:51:39.308
These hostiles we are up against possess
technology so far superior to our own,


00:51:39.349 --> 00:51:41.518
we don't have the faintest idea
how it works.


00:51:41.602 --> 00:51:45.105
We would all be much better off
if the stargate had been left in the ground.


00:51:45.189 --> 00:51:47.983
With respect, sir, we can't bury
our heads in the sand.


00:51:48.066 --> 00:51:51.153
I mean, think of how much we could learn.
Think of what we could bring back.


00:51:51.236 --> 00:51:54.740
What you could bring back is precisely
what I'm afraid of, Captain.


00:51:54.823 --> 00:51:58.202
However, the President of the
United States happens to agree with you.


00:51:58.285 --> 00:52:01.914
In the event your theories pan out, he
has ordered the formation of nine teams,


00:52:01.997 --> 00:52:04.958
whose duties will be to perform
reconnaissance, determine threats,


00:52:05.042 --> 00:52:08.837
and if possible, to make peaceful contact
with the peoples of these worlds.


00:52:08.921 --> 00:52:12.174
Now, these teams will operate
on a covert, top-secret basis.


00:52:12.216 --> 00:52:16.845
No one will know of their existence,
except the President and the joint chiefs.


00:52:16.887 --> 00:52:18.388
- Colonel O'Neill.
- Sir?


00:52:18.472 --> 00:52:20.557
Your team will be designated SG-1.


00:52:20.641 --> 00:52:22.643
The team will consist of yourself,
Captain Carter...


00:52:22.726 --> 00:52:23.977
And me?


00:52:24.978 --> 00:52:27.523
Dr. Jackson, we need you
to work as a consultant


00:52:27.606 --> 00:52:29.358
with the other SG teams from here.


00:52:29.399 --> 00:52:32.277
Your expertise in ancient cultures
and languages are far too valuable...


00:52:32.361 --> 00:52:34.822
I really have to be on their team.


00:52:36.448 --> 00:52:39.368
My wife is out there, General. I need to go.


00:52:43.580 --> 00:52:45.374
I'll take that under consideration.


00:52:45.415 --> 00:52:47.960
Major Kawalsky, you will head SG-2.


00:52:48.252 --> 00:52:49.294
I will?


00:52:49.378 --> 00:52:52.297
Colonel O'Neill keeps telling me
it's about time you had a command.


00:52:52.381 --> 00:52:54.591
I had a moment of weakness.


00:53:00.931 --> 00:53:02.975
Ferretti is conscious, sir.


00:53:04.601 --> 00:53:05.978
Dismissed.


00:53:12.359 --> 00:53:14.319
I'll take over. Thanks.


00:53:14.903 --> 00:53:16.280
- Ferretti.
- Hey.


00:53:17.114 --> 00:53:18.866
Listen, Ferretti.


00:53:19.074 --> 00:53:23.579
I know you're probably not feeling so hot,
but we need something from you.


00:53:27.833 --> 00:53:30.669
Looks like
he's way ahead of you, Colonel.


00:53:40.971 --> 00:53:43.056
You saw all seven symbols?


00:53:43.140 --> 00:53:45.559
This is where they went? You sure?


00:53:50.564 --> 00:53:51.815
Colonel, I'd like to remind you,


00:53:51.899 --> 00:53:55.027
in the event that you fail to notify
base camp within 24 hours,


00:53:55.110 --> 00:53:58.238
SG-2 will scrub the mission,
and return without you.


00:53:58.322 --> 00:53:59.615
Understood!


00:53:59.656 --> 00:54:03.202
Not gonna happen, Colonel.
SG-2 won't leave without you.


00:54:03.702 --> 00:54:05.537
All right, let's confirm transmitter codes.


00:54:05.621 --> 00:54:08.081
Remember, only the right code
will open the iris,


00:54:08.123 --> 00:54:10.709
and if you lose the transmitter,
you cannot get home.


00:54:10.792 --> 00:54:11.877
Understood, sir.


00:54:11.960 --> 00:54:13.921
Chevron seven unlocked.


00:54:22.513 --> 00:54:24.097
Let's move out.


00:54:28.769 --> 00:54:29.978
Kind of wish I was going with you.


00:54:30.020 --> 00:54:32.898
Yeah?
I'm kind of glad you're staying behind.


00:55:08.684 --> 00:55:09.768
Damn.


00:55:17.067 --> 00:55:18.735
Dammit, it's cold!


00:55:20.571 --> 00:55:23.365
Okay, people, let's get the gear out!
Let's move!


00:55:28.036 --> 00:55:30.205
Does anybody have a Kleenex?


00:55:44.678 --> 00:55:45.804
Come.


00:55:47.806 --> 00:55:49.057
No! No!


00:55:50.893 --> 00:55:51.852
No!


00:55:55.772 --> 00:55:57.566
This one has spirit.


00:56:52.162 --> 00:56:54.331
Does she please you, my love?


00:58:06.361 --> 00:58:08.238
It must be some sort
of ceremonial place.


00:58:08.322 --> 00:58:12.326
The gate is, has to be, an integral
part of their spiritual culture.


00:58:12.409 --> 00:58:14.870
See, this place was built for worshippers.


00:58:14.912 --> 00:58:19.374
Well, let's just try to be on our way
before the worshippees show up, huh?


00:58:19.875 --> 00:58:22.211
You figure out yet how to align
this gate to get back home?


00:58:22.294 --> 00:58:24.338
Yeah.
The device is the same as on Abydos.


00:58:24.421 --> 00:58:26.423
- This symbol represents...
- Brief Kawalsky's team yet?


00:58:26.507 --> 00:58:29.343
- Yes. This symbol represents...
- Good job.


00:58:32.471 --> 00:58:35.015
We'll have to set up camp where
there's better cover, Colonel.


00:58:35.098 --> 00:58:37.184
Sirs, I found what looks like a trail
down the mountain.


00:58:37.267 --> 00:58:39.061
Looks like it's seen traffic
in the last couple of days.


00:58:39.102 --> 00:58:41.480
Thank you, Airman. Carter?


00:58:42.064 --> 00:58:45.359
I set up a line of Claymores along
that ridge at 10 meter intervals.


00:58:45.400 --> 00:58:47.027
That sound about right, Kawalsky?


00:58:47.110 --> 00:58:48.821
Yeah. That'll work.


00:59:05.254 --> 00:59:08.090
This looks like a good spot right up here!


00:59:19.977 --> 00:59:24.148
- All right. If we're not back in 20 hours...
- We'll come rescue your sorry asses.


00:59:24.231 --> 00:59:25.232
Negative.


00:59:25.315 --> 00:59:28.402
You'll go back through the gate
with the combination Daniel just gave you,


00:59:28.443 --> 00:59:30.445
- as you were ordered.
- Yes, sir.


00:59:30.487 --> 00:59:33.031
If we don't make it back,
it's 'cause we got our butts kicked,


00:59:33.115 --> 00:59:36.076
- and that means you're out of here.
- Yes, sir.


00:59:37.161 --> 00:59:40.164
- Hold down the fort.
- Pick me up a T-shirt.


00:59:48.881 --> 00:59:51.967
So, Dr. Jackson,
tell me more about Sha're.


00:59:52.050 --> 00:59:54.386
- How did you meet?
- Sha're? Well, she's...


00:59:54.469 --> 00:59:55.512
She was a gift.


00:59:55.596 --> 00:59:59.808
She was, actually, from the elders
of Abydos the first night we were there.


00:59:59.850 --> 01:00:01.977
- And you accepted?
- Hold up!


01:00:02.478 --> 01:00:03.562
What?


01:00:10.819 --> 01:00:12.863
- See any weapons?
- No, sir.


01:00:20.662 --> 01:00:22.414
They're worshippers.


01:00:26.793 --> 01:00:29.796
All right, Captain,
take a position 50 yards...


01:00:30.881 --> 01:00:32.883
For crying out loud.


01:00:33.759 --> 01:00:35.761
The man has not changed.


01:00:36.512 --> 01:00:37.513
Hi.


01:00:39.848 --> 01:00:42.309
We just came through the stargate...


01:00:43.060 --> 01:00:46.230
The chaapa 'ai?


01:00:49.525 --> 01:00:52.486
No, please don't do that.


01:00:53.195 --> 01:00:55.072
- Friends of yours?
- No.


01:00:55.989 --> 01:00:57.574
Unless we want to get ourselves
a really bad reputation,


01:00:57.658 --> 01:01:02.246
I just think we should avoid shooting
the first people we meet on a new planet.


01:01:02.329 --> 01:01:05.207
Please, you don't have to do this.


01:01:15.133 --> 01:01:18.929
"Choose. " They want to know
if we're here to choose.


01:01:22.140 --> 01:01:25.185
Sure. We can choose. Choosing is good.


01:01:29.565 --> 01:01:31.859
It's a derivation of Arabic, combined with...


01:01:31.900 --> 01:01:33.485
Yeah, yeah, all right, whatever.


01:01:33.569 --> 01:01:37.072
Just ask them to take us
to the nearest village or town.


01:01:37.906 --> 01:01:41.952
Would you take us to...
Would you take us to...


01:01:45.455 --> 01:01:48.041
Chulak. Chulak.


01:01:51.753 --> 01:01:52.921
Chulak, eh?


01:02:11.064 --> 01:02:12.065
Chulak.


01:02:21.492 --> 01:02:24.620
Chulak. Sounds good.


01:02:25.704 --> 01:02:28.207
I hear it's nice this time of year.


01:03:48.328 --> 01:03:51.582
- Why are they treating us like this?
- They think we're gods.


01:03:53.667 --> 01:03:55.043
Incredible.


01:03:56.503 --> 01:04:00.591
This is a feast of some kind.
Apparently, someone's been expected.


01:04:02.718 --> 01:04:06.471
Okay. We're gods. Now what?


01:04:06.972 --> 01:04:08.515
I have no idea.


01:04:09.391 --> 01:04:13.020
Maybe you should tell them
we want to look around, Daniel.


01:04:27.701 --> 01:04:29.203
When in Rome...


01:04:58.398 --> 01:04:59.608
Behold,


01:05:03.695 --> 01:05:05.072
your queen.


01:05:08.784 --> 01:05:09.993
Sha're?


01:05:14.248 --> 01:05:18.460
- Sha're, thank God, I thought we'd never...
- Kneel before your queen!


01:05:20.212 --> 01:05:21.755
Sha're, it's me!


01:05:40.566 --> 01:05:42.818
Daniel. Daniel.


01:05:42.860 --> 01:05:44.903
- Sha're!
- Easy.


01:05:44.987 --> 01:05:46.822
- You've been unconscious for hours.
- No. I saw her.


01:05:46.864 --> 01:05:49.324
- I know. We all did.
- I saw Sha're.


01:05:51.743 --> 01:05:54.913
- Where are we?
- Some sort of prison.


01:05:59.585 --> 01:06:02.546
Come on, sit down. Sit down. Easy.


01:06:10.012 --> 01:06:11.138
It all happened so fast.


01:06:11.180 --> 01:06:15.350
I mean, Ra sent you flying across
the room, a guard zapped the colonel.


01:06:15.434 --> 01:06:16.560
Next thing I remember, we're all here.


01:06:16.643 --> 01:06:19.062
No, it wasn't Ra. It was Apophis.


01:06:19.188 --> 01:06:20.272
Who?


01:06:21.398 --> 01:06:25.194
It's from Egyptian mythology.
Ra was the sun god who ruled the day.


01:06:25.235 --> 01:06:27.571
Apophis was the serpent god,
Ra's rival, who ruled the night.


01:06:27.654 --> 01:06:31.283
It's right out of The Book of the Dead.
They're living it.


01:06:34.745 --> 01:06:36.413
What's he done to Sha're?
I've got to find her.


01:06:37.539 --> 01:06:38.916
We can't.


01:06:39.708 --> 01:06:43.462
- If I could just...
- Daniel, you saw her eyes.


01:06:43.754 --> 01:06:46.965
- Well, maybe it's some kind of drug...
- These hostiles are parasites.


01:06:47.049 --> 01:06:49.510
They use human beings as hosts.
That's what Ra did. That...


01:06:49.551 --> 01:06:53.055
No, I don't believe that.
I'm sorry, I just... I can't.


01:06:56.225 --> 01:06:59.228
If there's a way out of here,
I haven't found it yet.


01:06:59.311 --> 01:07:00.896
But look what I did find.


01:07:00.979 --> 01:07:04.650
- Daniel! You're okay!
- I think so.


01:07:06.235 --> 01:07:07.736
Easy, big guy.


01:07:09.029 --> 01:07:10.697
Welcome back
to the land of the conscious.


01:07:10.781 --> 01:07:12.074
O'Neer told me about Sha're.


01:07:12.157 --> 01:07:15.327
- Jack, help me. We can find her again.
- Daniel.


01:07:15.619 --> 01:07:16.787
Don't.


01:07:20.374 --> 01:07:23.836
Look, get some rest.
By all rights, you should be dead.


01:07:28.715 --> 01:07:30.509
- You still got that transmitter?
- Yeah.


01:07:30.592 --> 01:07:32.302
All right, we may have to destroy it.


01:07:32.386 --> 01:07:35.764
If we can't find a way out of here,
the mission's a bust anyway,


01:07:35.806 --> 01:07:39.143
and we don't want Apockhead or whatever
his name is to get his hands on that thing.


01:07:39.226 --> 01:07:43.480
Well, he still wouldn't know the code.
There's half a billion permutations.


01:07:44.273 --> 01:07:48.694
Don't take this personally, but
they're way smarter than we are.


01:07:51.572 --> 01:07:53.740
Come on, Skaara,
let's find a way out of here.


01:07:55.909 --> 01:07:57.369
What is this?


01:07:58.162 --> 01:08:00.706
It's a watch. It tells me the time.


01:08:05.961 --> 01:08:07.713
Where are you from?


01:08:09.006 --> 01:08:11.550
Earth. Chicago, if you wanna be...


01:08:11.633 --> 01:08:15.137
Your words mean nothing.
Where are you from?


01:08:15.220 --> 01:08:16.805
Excuse me.


01:08:19.975 --> 01:08:21.977
This is where we're from.


01:08:39.661 --> 01:08:41.288
Friendly fellow.


01:08:41.830 --> 01:08:44.249
What do you think that was about?


01:08:44.458 --> 01:08:45.918
I don't know.


01:08:49.171 --> 01:08:50.714
Come on, Skaara.


01:09:00.265 --> 01:09:02.684
Warren, let's go! Rise and shine!


01:09:03.519 --> 01:09:07.439
The sun is... The suns are coming up.
We're gonna be all right.


01:09:08.857 --> 01:09:10.818
We can't go through another night
like that, Major.


01:09:10.859 --> 01:09:14.154
Yeah. Gets a little chilly
on this planet at night.


01:09:14.488 --> 01:09:17.574
The Colonel should've sent us
a message by now.


01:09:17.699 --> 01:09:19.993
When do you have to make the decision


01:09:20.035 --> 01:09:22.871
whether or not to go back
to the stargate?


01:09:22.955 --> 01:09:25.290
That'll be about when hell freezes over.


01:09:25.374 --> 01:09:27.292
I think that pretty much describes
our current situation.


01:09:27.376 --> 01:09:28.919
We are not leaving here
without the Colonel.


01:09:29.002 --> 01:09:30.712
Is that understood?


01:09:44.184 --> 01:09:48.438
General, the warhead is armed
and ready for you to give the word, sir.


01:09:48.522 --> 01:09:50.816
How much time have we got left?


01:09:51.233 --> 01:09:53.110
Just under five hours.


01:09:53.735 --> 01:09:57.406
Let's keep our fingers off the trigger
until the time comes, shall we?


01:09:57.489 --> 01:09:58.740
Yes, sir.


01:10:13.797 --> 01:10:16.717
- Sha're is dead?
- Yeah.


01:10:17.217 --> 01:10:18.218
No.


01:10:19.469 --> 01:10:22.473
- Know what, Skaara? I don't know.
- We will save her.


01:10:22.556 --> 01:10:24.516
I can't promise you anything
at the moment.


01:10:24.600 --> 01:10:26.560
But you are a great warrior!
We defeated Ra together!


01:10:26.602 --> 01:10:30.063
Yeah, I know, but look around here.
Look what we're up against.


01:10:36.695 --> 01:10:38.071
We'll try.


01:10:41.492 --> 01:10:42.701
Come on.


01:11:02.012 --> 01:11:03.597
What did he say?


01:11:03.972 --> 01:11:05.974
They're going to choose.


01:11:06.183 --> 01:11:07.601
Choose what?


01:11:09.144 --> 01:11:11.772
Who will be the children of the gods.


01:11:38.841 --> 01:11:40.092
Sha're.


01:11:40.175 --> 01:11:41.343
Jack, help me, please.


01:11:41.426 --> 01:11:43.887
- Daniel!
- Daniel! Don't! Don't!


01:11:56.984 --> 01:11:59.069
Kneel before your masters!


01:12:21.216 --> 01:12:22.551
Skaara.


01:13:34.832 --> 01:13:36.041
Daniel!


01:13:38.460 --> 01:13:39.962
This one is passionate.


01:13:40.045 --> 01:13:41.338
How much would I remember
if you chose me?


01:13:41.421 --> 01:13:43.924
- Daniel, what are you doing?
- Tell me.


01:13:46.969 --> 01:13:49.429
Something of the host must survive.


01:13:50.347 --> 01:13:51.598
Nothing.


01:14:09.283 --> 01:14:10.325
Him.


01:14:14.788 --> 01:14:16.498
Skaara!


01:14:17.499 --> 01:14:21.378
O'Neer! O'Neer! O'Neer!


01:14:33.432 --> 01:14:34.933
Kill the rest.


01:15:00.542 --> 01:15:02.544
I can save these people!


01:15:04.922 --> 01:15:06.173
Help me.


01:15:10.719 --> 01:15:12.554
Many have said that.


01:15:19.937 --> 01:15:22.898
But you are the first I believe could do it!


01:15:45.504 --> 01:15:47.256
Get out of the way!


01:15:57.683 --> 01:15:59.393
Come on, let's move!


01:16:05.941 --> 01:16:08.068
Let's go, let's go, come on!


01:16:29.798 --> 01:16:31.466
You gonna be okay?


01:16:44.646 --> 01:16:46.023
Hey! Come on!


01:16:50.736 --> 01:16:52.571
I have nowhere to go.


01:16:53.906 --> 01:16:56.825
For this, you can stay at my place!
Let's go!


01:17:01.622 --> 01:17:03.290
What's your name?


01:17:03.832 --> 01:17:04.833
Teal'c.


01:17:04.917 --> 01:17:07.669
Teal'c, where will they
take Skaara, the boy?


01:17:07.753 --> 01:17:08.795
To the stargate.


01:17:08.879 --> 01:17:13.217
After they've selected hosts for
their children, they will return home.


01:17:24.686 --> 01:17:27.022
Sir, they have just under an hour
until the deadline.


01:17:27.064 --> 01:17:29.024
We should've heard from them by now.


01:17:29.066 --> 01:17:31.610
A lot can happen in an hour, Major.


01:17:32.486 --> 01:17:35.697
Okay, come on, people!
We're almost there! Let's go!


01:17:35.739 --> 01:17:37.991
We've got less than an hour.
How're we doing?


01:17:38.033 --> 01:17:40.035
We lost a few when we reached the forest.


01:17:40.118 --> 01:17:42.162
They will be hunted down and killed.


01:17:42.246 --> 01:17:45.415
Anyone who does not exist
to serve the gods is their enemy.


01:17:45.499 --> 01:17:47.292
And that makes you...


01:17:48.335 --> 01:17:51.630
I am a Jaffa.
Bred to serve, that they may live.


01:17:52.464 --> 01:17:54.216
I don't understand.


01:18:00.389 --> 01:18:01.765
Man!


01:18:03.392 --> 01:18:04.852
What the hell is that?


01:18:04.935 --> 01:18:08.355
It is an infant Goa'uld,
the larval form of the gods.


01:18:08.438 --> 01:18:12.359
I have carried one since I was a child,
as all Jaffa carry one.


01:18:14.611 --> 01:18:16.947
This is the twelfth I have carried.


01:18:17.030 --> 01:18:19.032
Well, get it out of there!


01:18:20.993 --> 01:18:24.246
In exchange for carrying
the infant Goa'uld until maturity,


01:18:24.329 --> 01:18:27.374
a Jaffa receives perfect health
and long life.


01:18:27.958 --> 01:18:31.295
If I were to remove it,
I would eventually die.


01:18:32.588 --> 01:18:35.340
Well, if I were you, I'd take my chances.


01:18:36.175 --> 01:18:37.468
Why did you do this?


01:18:37.551 --> 01:18:40.471
The Goa'uld are conquerors, nothing more.


01:18:40.929 --> 01:18:43.390
Not worthy of worship or sacrifice.


01:18:43.432 --> 01:18:46.602
You are the first to come along
with powers that approach theirs.


01:18:46.685 --> 01:18:47.936
Powers?


01:18:48.145 --> 01:18:51.607
You are strong,
perhaps strong enough to destroy them.


01:19:01.450 --> 01:19:03.994
All right, people! Let's go! Let's move!


01:19:07.122 --> 01:19:09.958
The boy you seek is no longer who he was.


01:19:11.251 --> 01:19:13.212
I don't wanna hear that.


01:20:07.516 --> 01:20:09.434
Take cover! Take cover!


01:20:46.138 --> 01:20:48.557
Colonel, we're sitting ducks here!


01:21:00.194 --> 01:21:01.445
Hold on.


01:21:06.074 --> 01:21:07.409
Now, fire!


01:21:37.272 --> 01:21:39.900
- Kawalsky?
- Kawalsky.


01:21:41.819 --> 01:21:43.111
Yeah!


01:21:44.738 --> 01:21:46.240
- Come on, folks!
- Come on, people!


01:21:46.323 --> 01:21:47.741
Up the hill!


01:21:57.459 --> 01:21:58.836
Great shot.


01:21:59.962 --> 01:22:02.172
- How many are there?
- A dozen, maybe more.


01:22:02.256 --> 01:22:03.423
They're going back through the gate.


01:22:03.465 --> 01:22:04.842
What about Skaara?


01:22:04.925 --> 01:22:06.426
He's with them.


01:22:13.809 --> 01:22:15.936
Warren! Casey! On my right!


01:22:26.488 --> 01:22:28.115
- No.
- Wait, sir.


01:22:30.826 --> 01:22:32.035
Skaara!


01:22:41.587 --> 01:22:42.838
Skaara.


01:23:20.125 --> 01:23:22.252
- Did you see the symbols?
- No.


01:23:25.672 --> 01:23:28.634
Sir, we got hostiles
coming out of the trees!


01:23:32.387 --> 01:23:34.473
Okay, people,
we're going on a little fieldtrip!


01:23:34.556 --> 01:23:37.684
Daniel, get busy on that stargate.
We got company.


01:23:37.768 --> 01:23:38.769
Captain, arm your Claymores.


01:23:38.852 --> 01:23:40.562
Me and Casey and Warren'll be
the last men out.


01:23:40.646 --> 01:23:45.484
Negative. That's my job.
Captain, help Daniel.


01:23:46.109 --> 01:23:48.195
Once you've sent the signal,
I want you to go through.


01:23:48.278 --> 01:23:49.780
Tell 'em we're bringing company.


01:23:49.863 --> 01:23:52.574
Let's go, move, move, move! Let's go!


01:23:59.498 --> 01:24:00.958
We can't hold 'em, sir!


01:24:01.041 --> 01:24:02.376
Pull 'em out!


01:24:02.417 --> 01:24:04.503
Fall back, fall back. Now.


01:24:11.260 --> 01:24:12.511
- Daniel.
- It's here.


01:24:12.594 --> 01:24:13.762
Go! Go!


01:24:17.266 --> 01:24:18.517
Come on!


01:24:22.312 --> 01:24:24.773
Send the signal
as soon as it opens, Captain.


01:24:36.994 --> 01:24:39.746
- Check the coordinates.
- Looking at 'em now.


01:24:40.497 --> 01:24:42.374
- No signal yet, General.
- Stand by.


01:24:44.585 --> 01:24:45.794
Wait! There it is.


01:24:46.545 --> 01:24:48.505
- Is it working?
- Let's hope so.


01:24:58.474 --> 01:25:00.184
Hit the Claymores!


01:25:06.523 --> 01:25:09.359
Captain, let's get these people
out of here now! Move!


01:25:09.443 --> 01:25:12.863
Give me a few seconds,
then start sending them through.


01:25:23.499 --> 01:25:24.875
Stand fast!


01:25:25.167 --> 01:25:27.628
Hold your fire! They're refugees!


01:25:28.253 --> 01:25:31.089
I hope you know
what you're doing, Captain.


01:25:33.717 --> 01:25:35.511
Go, go, go! Please!


01:25:46.897 --> 01:25:48.982
Go, go, go. Stop, stop, stop.


01:25:49.066 --> 01:25:51.568
Now, okay. Come on! Come on!


01:25:57.407 --> 01:25:58.492
Nice!


01:26:05.290 --> 01:26:06.667
That's it!


01:26:07.292 --> 01:26:08.293
Go!


01:26:12.005 --> 01:26:14.091
Casey, Warren, fall back!


01:26:20.180 --> 01:26:22.349
- They behind you?
- I hope so.


01:26:23.267 --> 01:26:24.518
Go! Go!


01:26:34.236 --> 01:26:35.445
Casey!


01:26:36.905 --> 01:26:38.198
Man down!


01:26:40.075 --> 01:26:42.953
Move! Come on, move your ass!


01:27:00.429 --> 01:27:02.389
- Hold your fire! Hold your fire!
- Hold your fire! Hold your fire!


01:27:02.473 --> 01:27:04.057
They're with us!


01:27:16.904 --> 01:27:19.072
Now! Lock it up! Lock it up!


01:27:34.922 --> 01:27:38.967
Got it. I got it. He's not breathing.
Let's go. Get him breathing.


01:27:55.776 --> 01:27:56.819
Sir?


01:28:01.990 --> 01:28:05.869
Colonel O'Neill, care to explain?


01:28:07.538 --> 01:28:11.250
We can use the stargate
to send these people home, sir.


01:28:12.584 --> 01:28:14.378
What's he doing here?


01:28:19.007 --> 01:28:24.680
General Hammond, this is Teal'c.
He can help us.


01:28:24.721 --> 01:28:25.889
Do you know what he is?


01:28:25.973 --> 01:28:29.476
Yes sir, I do.
He's the man who saved our lives.


01:28:30.853 --> 01:28:35.482
And if you accept my recommendation, sir,
he'll join SG-1.


01:28:37.234 --> 01:28:39.736
That decision may not be up to you.


01:28:40.195 --> 01:28:42.322
Let's go, man down. Stand back!


01:28:42.364 --> 01:28:45.701
Stand back!
All right, troop, get him off the ramp!


01:28:46.994 --> 01:28:49.121
Let's get him off the ramp.


01:29:01.091 --> 01:29:03.594
Colonel O'Neill, Major Kawalsky.


01:29:04.887 --> 01:29:10.225
The sure-to-be-very-interesting debriefing
of SG units 1 and 2 will be at 0730.


01:29:11.393 --> 01:29:12.644
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.


01:29:15.689 --> 01:29:19.276
All right, let's get these people situated.
This way.


01:29:29.244 --> 01:29:31.580
She's out there somewhere, Jack.


01:29:32.247 --> 01:29:34.750
I know. So's Skaara.


01:29:35.542 --> 01:29:37.169
So what do we do?


01:29:39.421 --> 01:29:40.839
We find 'em.

